S4 is implemented: generator expressions are now anonymous generators and the C1 inlining is gone. JVM and Node tests pass; Dart was not run because the compile command needed a permission this session couldn't get. Full findings are in `collab/1791096045000-compiler-engineer-python-c2-s4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md`.

**Changed files**
- `src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc`:
  - A generator expression, in parentheses or as the sole call argument, now lowers to `(let [%first (py/iter <outermost iterable>)] (py/make-generator "<genexpr>" (fn [%gen] ...)))`. The outermost iterable is evaluated and `iter()`-checked at creation in the enclosing scope; every other clause runs only when the generator is resumed.
  - The inlining is removed: `consuming-builtins`, `builtin?`, `callee-builtin`, the special case at the call site, the `:sum`/`:any`/`:all` comprehension kinds, and both "phase C2" refusals.
  - `yield` inside a generator expression is now the syntax error "'yield' inside generator expression".
- `src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc`:
  - Removed `py/genexp-unsupported`.
  - `sum`, `any`, `all` and `set` now take one element at a time instead of building a full list first. Without this, removing the inlining would break laziness and the existing C1 "sum stopped" / "set stopped" expectations.
  - The generator machinery is unchanged: every crossing still goes through `py/gen-switch`.
- `docs/design/yang.antlr.md`: the S4 table row now ends "Landed." Other places still say S4 is pending (the 8.5.3 intro sentence, the line-19 status paragraph, the list near line 3568). I left them because they were outside the allowed text.
- Tests:
  - `e2e_c2_test.clj` has six new source-program tests, with expected output checked against the local CPython 3.9.6. They cover laziness, the iterable being evaluated at creation, scoping, nesting and rebound consumers, PEP 479, and send/throw/close.
  - `prelude_parity_test.cljc` has two portable tests, including the recursion-limit boundary: under limit 2, a third nested generator expression is refused and stays `:created`.
  - `lower_test.clj` has a golden showing a generator expression passed to `sum` is a plain call with no inlining, plus new yield diagnostics and classification cases.
  - In `float_address_test.cljc` I re-minted five address goldens, last and once.
- Tests updated because they pinned the removed inlining:
  - In `lower_test.clj` I removed the two "generator expression (phase C2)" refusal rows; those refusals no longer exist.
  - In `e2e_c1_test.clj`, `generator-consumer-rebound-test` asserted the C1 `NotImplementedError`. It now asserts CPython's result: the rebound lambda receives the generator. That file wasn't on the allowed list; I relied on the brief's permission to update tests that pinned the removed inlining. No other C1 test changed.

